  "summary": "At a Springfield, Missouri city council meeting on Sept 22, 2026, Mayor Jeff Schrag moved a resolution to review the city's Flock ALPR contracts into committee and blocked public comment, then cleared the room. Police detained freelance photographer Noah Powell and later arrested resident Mia Hyder after she attempted to speak against Flock cameras during an unrelated public comment period. Springfield operates 41 Flock cameras.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "There was a resolution before the council that would trigger a review of the controversial camera systems, but Schrag moved to send the resolution to committee and prevent public comment on the issue.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "Springfield has 41 Flock cameras, according to the Flock Transparency Portal.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "All I'm trying to do is get people answers to some real questions that they've brought to us for months.",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
  ],
